  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tehran Solid Waste Management Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DON&apos;T PUB DROPPED  REHABILITATION AND IMPROVEMENTS TO FACILITIES, EQUIPMENT AND HANDLING PROCEDURES FOR MANAGING HAZARDOUS AND TOXIC WASTES FOCUSSED IN THE GEOGRAPHIC REGION NEAR TEHRAN. Please note:  Project title changed February 7, 2002 to: Tehran Solid Waste Management Project 11/21/06.  Task Team Leader changed from Allan Rotman to Hocine Chalal effective May 2006.  $1.0 million PPF closed in September 2006.  This operation is ready for appraisal and still held back because of the CAS having to be submitted to the Board prior to completing project preparation. 05/10/07.  In April 2007 the Bank received the Govt request to extend the PPF ($1.0m) closing date of February 2008 for one more year.  Although the PPF closing has elapsed, Management has indicated that it would be willing to consider favorably the request. An explanatory note is being prepared to the RVP to justify the retroactive extension of the closing date. 6/6/07.  The documentation for the retroactive extension of the closing date by one year is currently being processed. 8/31/07.  Request for extension the closing date to end-February 2008 has been granted.</narrative>
  </description>
